WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.491
Welcome to Part 5: right way, wrong way.

2
00:00:04.791 --> 00:00:11.039
By the end, you'll be able to open a box and tell in
seconds whether it's wired safely, which supply it has,

3
00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:17.249
and what a tripping breaker is telling you. And you'll
know the field card that's in every job's files.

4
00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:22.589
These two boxes look almost the same
when you open them. They're not.

5
00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:28.424
The wrong way. One wire feeds all three
injections, and there are no breakers.

6
00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:33.014
The supply has 25 amps behind that
one wire. If one group shorts,

7
00:00:33.014 --> 00:00:36.828
nothing shuts off. The wire
just keeps getting hotter.

8
00:00:37.978 --> 00:00:42.651
The right way. Each group has its
own wire, on its own 4 amp breaker.

9
00:00:42.951 --> 00:00:45.684
If one group shorts,
that one breaker trips.

10
00:00:45.684 --> 00:00:49.787
The other groups stay lit, and
you know exactly where to look.

11
00:00:50.937 --> 00:00:53.983
So when you open a box,
ask three questions.

12
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:58.046
One. Is there a breaker for
every wire leaving the box?

13
00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:02.297
Two. Does each wire go to one
injection only? Follow it.

14
00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:06.498
If it splits, it's wrong,
even if both groups are small.

15
00:01:06.798 --> 00:01:11.149
Three. Is every light circuit
breaker 4 amps? Bigger is wrong.

16
00:01:11.449 --> 00:01:14.793
Any answer is no? Don't change
it, and don't add to it.

17
00:01:14.793 --> 00:01:17.292
Take photos, and call your crew lead.

18
00:01:18.442 --> 00:01:22.916
Next, read the supply
label. We use two sizes.

19
00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:27.154
600 watt, and 450 watt, both at 24 volts.

20
00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:30.927
Each circuit follows
the same rules on both.

21
00:01:30.927 --> 00:01:34.334
4 amps, 96 watts, 70 lights at the most.

22
00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:40.295
The difference is the total. A
600 watt supply can push 25 amps.

23
00:01:40.295 --> 00:01:43.198
A 450 watt supply, about 18.8.

24
00:01:43.498 --> 00:01:47.401
So on a 450 watt box,
add up every circuit.

25
00:01:47.401 --> 00:01:52.824
Five circuits of 60 lights is
about 411 watts. That fits.

26
00:01:53.124 --> 00:01:58.643
Five circuits of 70 is about 480 watts.
That's more than the supply can give,

27
00:01:58.643 --> 00:02:02.691
even though every single
circuit is inside its limit.

28
00:02:02.991 --> 00:02:07.109
Asked to add lights to a 450
watt box? Total it first.

29
00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:12.925
Over about 328 lights on Pure White,
it doesn't fit. Tell your crew lead.

30
00:02:14.075 --> 00:02:18.133
Now, a tripping breaker is good
news. It means the safety is working.

31
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.265
It's telling you that
circuit has too much on it.

32
00:02:21.565 --> 00:02:26.905
So fix the circuit. Count the lights
first. It's almost always more than 70.

33
00:02:27.205 --> 00:02:30.499
Never fit a bigger breaker.
It doesn't fix anything.

34
00:02:30.499 --> 00:02:33.155
It just lets more amps into thin wire.

35
00:02:34.305 --> 00:02:40.106
Last, the field card. You'll find it in
every job's files. Open it on any job.

36
00:02:40.406 --> 00:02:47.221
The numbers. 60 lights a circuit,
70 at the most. 4 amps, 96 watts.

37
00:02:47.221 --> 00:02:53.167
At least 22.8 volts at the
last light. 16/2 FT-4 feeder.

38
00:02:53.467 --> 00:03:01.635
The box. 600 watt or 450 watt. On a
450, keep the total under 450 watts.

39
00:03:01.935 --> 00:03:06.462
And meter it before you leave.
With everything on PW, full bright.

40
00:03:06.762 --> 00:03:15.334
Amps, with the clamp meter, on the positive feeder of
each circuit, at the box. Under 3.6 amps is a pass.

41
00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:23.585
3.6 to 4 is tight: it works, but note it, so nobody
adds lights later. Over 4 is a fail. Split it.

42
00:03:23.885 --> 00:03:29.077
Volts, with the multimeter. About
24 volts at the supply output,

43
00:03:29.077 --> 00:03:36.548
and 22.8 or more at the last light of every
group. Under 22.8, move the injection closer.

44
00:03:37.698 --> 00:03:38.722
Let's lock it in.

45
00:03:39.022 --> 00:03:43.533
Wrong way: one wire, no
breakers, nothing shuts off.

46
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:47.167
Right way: own wire, own 4 amp breaker.

47
00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:52.646
Three questions when you open a box.
Any no? Photos, and call your crew lead.

48
00:03:52.946 --> 00:03:58.329
Read the supply label. On a 450
watt box, total every circuit.

49
00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:02.030
A trip means count the lights.
Never a bigger breaker.

50
00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:06.496
Next, take the Part 5 quiz.
Part 6 is how to test it.
